  "lineage": "Early-1990s UK electronic subgenre developed in 1990-1993 London through synthesis of Belgian new-beat, Detroit techno, and US house with chopped-Amen-break percussion, ragga-MC vocal-sampling, and rapidly-accelerating tempo (138-150 BPM and rising toward jungle's 170+). The 1991 Acen \"Trip to the Moon\", 1992 SL2 \"On a Ragga Tip\", and the broader Production House and Suburban Base label rosters consolidated the canonical sound. Direct ancestor of jungle and drum-and-bass.",
